	(text "PCA9685 #2, I2C address 0x41 (A0 high). Outputs drive the power bar inputs at 3.3 V\nlike the Robo-Tank v3 GPIOs. /OE fixed to GND, see PCA9685 #1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "34a33485-269c-41e1-8ebd-90ddaa71930d")
	)
	(text "Backup floats in series with power bar 1 outlets 1 and 2 (open float = outlet OFF via the pull-down;\nbridge with a wire when unused). Note: Robo-Tank v3 labels them AC1 = outlet 2, AC2 = outlet 1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "49580b22-7a92-4bf3-807f-aafa8f9005f2")
	)
	(text "Box headers for the IDC DB9 adapter cable (wires 1..9 -> DB9 pins 1,6,2,7,3,8,4,9,5;\nDB9: 1..4 = Ch1..4, 5 = GND, 6..9 = Ch8..5 as Robo-Tank v3). Verify on the first sample.\nPin 10 (not wired by the DB9 adapter) = +3V3_EXT: feeder dual use - an Eheim feeder (Robo-Tank mod:\n+3.3 V / Signal / GND) connects via its own cable to pins 10 / any channel / 9; that channel then drives\nthe feeder instead of an outlet. Signal is a 3.3 V push-pull PCA output (about 10 mA)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 189.23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9fb42181-f1a6-4da3-982c-dd53eb78c614")
	)
